WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.596 --> 00:00:17.362
"Get these out of here!"

2
00:00:17.703 --> 00:00:18.983
cried Professor Flashback.

3
00:00:20.344 --> 00:00:23.325
Several dinosaurs jumped onto a table and knocked over equipment.

4
00:00:24.826 --> 00:00:26.526
A small clock fell down and broke.

5
00:00:27.827 --> 00:00:29.848
Another dinosaur ate books from the bookshelf.

6
00:00:30.988 --> 00:00:32.989
"They're destroying my laboratory!"

7
00:00:33.909 --> 00:00:35.709
Professor Flashback pulled at his hair.

8
00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:39.150
Roxy saw a big dinosaur bump into the big clock.

9
00:00:40.051 --> 00:00:40.971
The clock rocked.

10
00:00:41.991 --> 00:00:42.731
Roxy gulped.

11
00:00:42.751 --> 00:00:47.613
"If that clock breaks, Metro City will be trapped in the past!"

12
00:00:48.693 --> 00:00:50.273
She darted to the clock and grabbed it.

13
00:00:51.214 --> 00:00:54.735
The clock's big hand was pointing to the year 65 million BC.

14
00:00:54.755 --> 00:00:58.816
"Shoo!" said Professor Flashback.

15
00:00:59.648 --> 00:01:02.130
He was pushing three small dinosaurs away with a broom.

16
00:01:03.271 --> 00:01:05.233
He suddenly spotted Roxy near the clock.

17
00:01:06.154 --> 00:01:07.034
"What are you doing?"

18
00:01:07.214 --> 00:01:07.715
he yelled.

19
00:01:08.716 --> 00:01:09.717
Roxy glared at him.

20
00:01:09.737 --> 00:01:12.539
"I'm bringing Metro City back to the present!"

21
00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.201
She grabbed the clock's hand.

22
00:01:15.221 --> 00:01:18.424
"No!" cried Professor Flashback.

23
00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:20.165
"Do not—oof!"

24
00:01:21.266 --> 00:01:23.208
A fat dinosaur knocked the professor down.

25
00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:25.590
Roxy yanked the clock's hand.

26
00:01:26.511 --> 00:01:27.611
She turned it to the present.

27
00:01:33.692 --> 00:01:35.253
Electricity shot through the lab.

28
00:01:38.635 --> 00:01:40.756
In a moment the electricity was gone.

29
00:01:41.717 --> 00:01:42.958
And so were the dinosaurs.

30
00:01:43.998 --> 00:01:45.159
Roxy took a deep breath.

31
00:01:45.859 --> 00:01:49.542
"Whew!" Professor Flashback grinned.

32
00:01:49.562 --> 00:01:52.343
"Thanks for saving my clock," he said.

33
00:01:53.124 --> 00:01:54.485
Roxy turned back to the clock.

34
00:01:55.485 --> 00:01:59.748
Whiz-hoo! Her eye laser beams blew the clock into a million pieces.

35
00:02:01.076 --> 00:02:03.737
"No!" the professor cried.

36
00:02:03.757 --> 00:02:07.178
"That clock is dangerous," said Roxy.

37
00:02:07.198 --> 00:02:11.039
"And you, Professor Flashback, are in big trouble."

38
00:02:11.979 --> 00:02:13.800
The professor narrowed his eyes at Roxy.

39
00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:15.760
He pulled his sleeve up.

40
00:02:16.740 --> 00:02:18.621
A small golden watch was on his wrist.

41
00:02:18.641 --> 00:02:22.442
"Good-bye, Rocket Girl," said Professor Flashback.

42
00:02:23.322 --> 00:02:24.662
He pressed a button on his watch.

43
00:02:26.383 --> 00:02:30.344
Za-wap! Electricity flashed and the professor disappeared!

44
00:02:31.432 --> 00:02:32.513
Roxy scratched her head.

45
00:02:32.533 --> 00:02:35.174
"I wonder where he went."

46
00:02:36.674 --> 00:02:39.736
The next day Roxy and her friends were at the Natural History Museum.

47
00:02:40.616 --> 00:02:42.957
Lots of fossils and dinosaur bones were on display.

48
00:02:42.977 --> 00:02:45.518
"Wow!" said Jack.

49
00:02:45.538 --> 00:02:46.519
"A T.

50
00:02:46.659 --> 00:02:47.739
rex skeleton!"

51
00:02:50.941 --> 00:02:51.801
Mara smiled.

52
00:02:52.421 --> 00:02:55.003
"It's a lot less scary than a live T.

53
00:02:55.123 --> 00:02:57.864
rex." Roxy pretended to sigh.

54
00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:01.762
"I can't believe I missed those dinosaurs."

55
00:03:02.803 --> 00:03:04.544
Terrell gave her a suspicious look.

56
00:03:07.946 --> 00:03:10.308
The friends saw a cave painting from the Stone Age.

57
00:03:11.249 --> 00:03:12.830
It showed cavemen hunting animals.

58
00:03:13.930 --> 00:03:15.912
One caveman looked different from the others.

59
00:03:15.932 --> 00:03:18.694
"Is that guy wearing a hat?"

60
00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:19.534
asked Terrell.

61
00:03:19.554 --> 00:03:22.096
"I think so," said Jack.

62
00:03:22.856 --> 00:03:25.178
"It looks like he has binoculars too."

63
00:03:25.198 --> 00:03:27.680
"That's weird," said Mara.

64
00:03:28.664 --> 00:03:30.606
"Binoculars didn't exist back then!"

65
00:03:31.748 --> 00:03:33.529
Roxy looked at the man and smiled.

66
00:03:37.053 --> 00:03:39.036
But she didn't say a word to her friends.
